  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd. Salim vs State Of U.P. Thru. Home Secy. Lko. And 2 ... on 12 November, 2025 Author: Abdul Moin Bench: Abdul Moin High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc-Lko:71973-Db High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Lucknow Criminal Misc. Writ Petition No. - 10526 of 2025 Mohd. Salim .....Petitioner(s) Versus State Of U.P. Thru. Home Secy. Lko. And 2 Others .....Respondent(s) Counsel for Petitioner(s) : Khaleeq Ahmad Khan Counsel for Respondent(s) Mohd. Salim vs State Of U.P. Thru. Home Secy. Lko.",
    "facts": "3. Instant writ petition has been filed praying for a writ of certiorari quashing the FIR No.33 of 2025 under Sections 318(2), 318(4), 274, 275, 111 B.N.S., 51, 59(i), 63, 57(2)(i) of the Food Safety & Standards Act, 2006, Police Station Madiyaon, District Lucknow. Upon he being caught, he also named the petitioner and several other persons to whom he was selling said adulterated tea leaves.",
    "arguments": "4. Contention of the learned counsel for the petitioner is that in an inspection conducted by the S.T.F. one Mohd Arif was caught making adulterated tea leaves. 5. Contention is that there is no evidence linking the petitioner with the main accused namely Mohd Arif and in case the respondents authorities are of the view that the petitioner has also indulged in selling the adulterated tea leaves, it was always open for the respondents authorities to have conducted an inspection and arrived at the said finding but certainly on the basis of the petitioner being named by the main accused he cannot be roped in the said FIR and on the basis of the same being harassed. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Contention of the learned counsel for the petitioner is that in an inspection conducted by the S.T.F. one Mohd Arif was caught making adulterated tea leaves. 5. Contention is that there is no evidence linking the petitioner with the main accused namely Mohd Arif and in case the respondents authorities are of the view that the petitioner has also indulged in selling the adulterated tea leaves, it was always open for the respondents authorities to have conducted an inspection and arrived at the said finding but certainly on the basis of the petitioner being named by the main accused he cannot be roped in the said FIR and on the basis of the same being harassed. 6.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
